const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Can you produce pants from our own size chart?",
    a: "A buyer size chart is a strong starting point for the brief. Once the chart or reference materials are received, the pattern approach, tolerances, and grading are evaluated and agreed per project before sampling, so later checks have a fixed reference. Whether the chart can be followed exactly or needs adjustment is confirmed at that stage rather than assumed.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which fabric makes sense for a first pants program?",
    a: "It depends on the use case and the market. Cotton twill and canvas directions suit casual and work builds, denim carries its own wash and construction rules, and knit fabrics such as french terry suit jogger directions. Fabric weight for the selected material is a required field in the brief, but the right value comes from the target use and season rather than from a generic range.",
  },
  {
    q: "How is shrinkage handled in washed pants?",
    a: "The pattern carries a shrinkage allowance based on how the selected fabric actually behaves in the intended wash, and that allowance is confirmed through testing per project. The sample is then measured after washing, not only at cutting, so the finished measurements match the chart. In production, a post-wash measurement checkpoint can be agreed in the inspection plan for the order.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can we add a leather patch, custom hardware, and branded trims?",
    a: "A leather or PU patch, custom zipper pull, button, rivet, or drawcord end can be proposed in the brief, but availability and suitability are not assumed. Share the artwork, size, material, attachment method, and target quantity for each item. We review sourcing, fabric compatibility, and minimums for the project before confirming which trims can be sampled and approved for bulk.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is checked on pants before packing?",
    a: "Measurements against the chart, waistband and fly symmetry, pocket position and attachment, reinforcement at the specified stress points, closure function, wash shade against the reference, labels, and packing details. The inspection plan and its tolerances are agreed per order and tied to the approved sample rather than applied as a fixed standard.",
  },
